{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1269725-trollhunters-in-exalted","id":1269725,"title":"Trollhunters in Exalted.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-21T19:33:44-08:00","id":1269725,"title":"Trollhunters in Exalted.","content":"So, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trollhunters\" target=\"_blank\">Trollhunters,</a> is a delightful YA TV series by Del Toro. One of hte central MCGuffins is the amulet of Merlin, a tool that transforms and allows Jim to use its armor and sword, as well as enhancing him.<br /> <br /> Now, for those who have seen it, does it sound more like an artifact with lots of evocations, or an actual Exigent style exaltation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T19:40:59-08:00","id":1269727,"title":"","content":"I'd say artifact with evocations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T22:12:46-08:00","id":1271378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1269725-trollhunters-in-exalted#post1269725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trollhunters\" target=\"_blank\">Trollhunters,</a> is a delightful YA TV series by Del Toro. One of hte central MCGuffins is the amulet of Merlin, a tool that transforms and allows Jim to use its armor and sword, as well as enhancing him.<br /> <br /> Now, for those who have seen it, does it sound more like an artifact with lots of evocations, or an actual Exigent style exaltation?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Stories like this really straddle the line between N/A artifact and some form of Exaltation. In this instance though, I'd lean more towards artifact simply because the powers are very physical, There are a few times were the amulet interacts with other assorted magical objects, but really it just gives Jim artifact armor and a daiklave (and later a thunderbolt shield and skycutters). Other than having an associated calling, it doesn't really make him super human.<br /> <br /> Conversely, I just started the new She-Ra today, and it seems much more like a Solar Exaltation channeled through a sword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T01:32:58-08:00","id":1271936,"title":"","content":"This thread's reminded me how much I've enjoyed that show and that the fac